# Extract: every stamp line of the qmd-watcher window 2026-10-15 09:27 -> 2026-10-26 15:51
# (witness for #3165's walk figures, filed by #3508)
#
# WHY AN EXTRACT EXISTS
# `agent-services/scripts/qmd-watcher.sh`'s cooldown cost block and `architecture/qmd.md`
# section 5 both state a no-op `qmd update` walk as `median 2 s, mean 1.8 s, max 39 s`,
# measured on 2026-10-22 off the watcher's own supervisor log. Neither surface had a
# committed copy of the sample behind those three numbers: the log is a 10 MB
# self-overwriting file, so the figures were re-derivable only while supervisord happened
# to still hold the window. This file is that sample.
# The source store is 10,485,795 bytes, over the `WITNESS_MAX_BYTES` = 1,048,576
# ceiling on what a demand may order, so it is never ordered whole. The stamp-line
# projection below is 38.0 % of that ceiling (398,795 of 1,048,576 bytes) and carries
# everything the three figures need; this file as committed is 38.6 % once this header is
# counted -- which is why the cheap thing to do was to commit it and the impossible thing
# is to try later.
#
# PROVENANCE
# Source store   : ~/lloyd-data/logs/services/agent-qmd-watcher.log.1
#                  (/home/alansrobotlab/lloyd-data/logs/services/agent-qmd-watcher.log.1)
#                  10,485,795 bytes, mtime 2026-10-26 15:51:04 -0700 = 2026-10-26T22:51:04Z.
#                  (`ls -la` on this box prints the first form; the box is UTC-7/UTC-8, so
#                  reading a rotation stamp off a listing is 7 or 8 hours off a UTC one.)
# Projection grep: grep -E '^[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2} (Change detected|Index updated|Watching )' /home/alansrobotlab/lloyd-data/logs/services/agent-qmd-watcher.log.1
#                  -> 8,357 lines / 398,795 bytes. Every body line below is one of
#                  those 8,357 lines, VERBATIM and in file order: nothing was
#                  reformatted, re-stamped, sorted, sampled or deduplicated, because a
#                  normalised copy would change the `wc -c` figure this file exists to pin.
# Composition    : 4,171 `Change detected` + 4,171 `Index updated` + 15
#                  `Watching` = the whole file's 8,357 stamp lines. A `Watching` line
#                  is the restart banner the watcher prints at startup, so those 15
#                  are the process boundaries inside this window.
# Window         : opened by the rotation that made .1 the live file -- its predecessor
#                  agent-qmd-watcher.log.2 carries mtime 2026-10-15 09:27:21 -0700 =
#                  2026-10-15T16:27:21Z -- and closed at .1's own mtime above, when
#                  supervisord rotated it again: 11 days 6 h 24 min between the two mtimes,
#                  11.27 days.
# Body bounds    : first line  `09:27:24 Index updated, embedding new documents...`
#                  last line   `15:51:03 Change detected, updating index...`
#                  The stamps carry no date, so the window's DATES come only from those two
#                  rotation mtimes. `2026-10-22`, in the file name and in the two prose
#                  surfaces, is the day the figures were computed, not the span they cover.
#
# PAIRING RULE -- the derivation the two prose surfaces describe
# One walk is the gap from an `HH:MM:SS Change detected` stamp to the NEXT `HH:MM:SS Index
# updated` stamp. Because the stamps carry no date the pairing drops two kinds of pair
# first: a NEGATIVE gap is a walk that crossed midnight, and a pair straddling a `Watching`
# restart banner is a gap between two processes rather than one walk.
# Stated honestly for THIS window: both rules remove nothing here. Zero negative gaps --
# the longest walk is 39 s and no walk landed across a midnight -- and zero pairs lost to a
# banner, because every `Change detected` below got its `Index updated` before the next
# banner. They are written out because the rule has to be correct for whatever window a
# reader applies it to next; nobody should infer from this file that the two drops are
# decoration.
# n is 4,170, one fewer than the 4,171 `Change detected` stamps, and the reason is the
# two bounds above: the window opens on an `Index updated` with no preceding `Change
# detected`, and closes on a `Change detected` whose walk's completion fell in the next
# file. Nothing was dropped to arithmetic.
# The script's cost block states NO cycle count on purpose, because its log is live and two
# passes an hour apart do not agree on n. Here n is reproducible forever: the body is
# frozen, which is the entire point of committing it.
#
# RE-DERIVE -- reads this file ALONE. No read under ~/lloyd-data is needed or wanted.
# EX=~/obsidian/backlog/data/2026-10-22.3165-services-agent-qmd-watcher.log
# 1.  wc -l -c < "$EX"                          #  8444   405323   (header + body)
# 2.  grep -v '^#' "$EX" | wc -l -c             # 8357 398795
# 3.  grep -v '^#' "$EX" \
#     | awk 'BEGIN{pen=-1} /^[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9] /{split($1,t,":"); s=t[1]*3600+t[2]*60+t[3]; if($2=="Change"){pen=s} else if($2=="Watching"){pen=-1} else if(pen>=0){d=s-pen; pen=-1; if(d>=0) print d}}' \
#     | sort -n \
#     | awk '{a[NR]=$1; sum+=$1; if($1==39)c++} END{n=NR; med=(n%2)? a[(n+1)/2] : (a[n/2]+a[n/2+1])/2.0; i=int(0.99*n+0.999999); if(i<1)i=1; printf "n=%d median=%.1f mean=%.4f max=%d p99=%d cycles_at_39s=%d\n", n, med, sum/n, a[n], a[i], c}'
#     Expected from the bytes committed here:
#       n=4170 median=2.0 mean=1.7583 max=39 p99=3 cycles_at_39s=1
# The first three of those ARE the published figures: `median 2 s`, `mean 1.8 s`,
# `max 39 s`. `mean=1.7583` is the unrounded form of the published `mean 1.8 s`, and no
# figure here is a new one: `p99=3` is printed because the same pass computes it, not
# because a third surface publishes it. `cycles_at_39s=1` is the tail the 60-second
# COOLDOWN_SEC is a floor under -- exactly one 39 s walk in 4,170, which is what makes a
# minute a 30x margin at a 2 s median rather than an arbitrary round number.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS NOT
# Not a mirror. Nothing under ~/lloyd-data was read-and-written-back to make it, and
# nothing here may be copied back. Not a live sample: the window closed at the 2026-10-26
# rotation. Whoever wants today's figure runs the projection grep above on whatever
# agent-qmd-watcher.log.1 holds then and applies the same pairing rule -- that is the
# re-runnable method the cost block points at; this file is the retained RESULT.
#
# Body: the 8,357 stamp lines below this header, verbatim.
